ingful statement.", "no free-surface / wave-body / ship-hull physics (declared in the module note).", "sub4 (5120 panels) rerun was still running at delivery; sub1/sub2/sub3 reproduced bit-identically."], "findings": {"F1_medium_report_order_arithmetic": {"base4_misread_reproduces_report": [0.949, 0.98, 0.992], "claim_in_subject_report": "observed order 0.95 / 0.98 / 0.99 for the integral added mass; conclusion 'the integral inherits the first-order per-panel flux'", "impact": "no effect on the reported added-mass errors or the <3% verdict; affects only the convergence interpretation and the subject's suggestion that README needed review.", "recomputed_p_log2": [1.897600491583338, 1.9599767499066434, 1.9830922992759135], "verdict": "FALSIFIED: with h halving per subdivision the integral added-mass order is ~2 (1.72/1.90/1.96/1.98), matching README 'near 2'; the subject's 0.95/0.98/0.99 are log4-space values. Per-panel flux is the ~1st-order quantity (0.94/1.09/1.09)."}, "F2_medium_registry_gap": {"action": "registered by this audit with the audited numbers (see insert_verdict.sql)", "claim": "tensor_benchmark_cases is the machine referee for this anchor", "measured": "0 rows for anchor_slug=CASE-BEM-SPHERE-ADDED-MASS before this audit (35 rows total in table)"}, "F3_low_cluster_claim": {"claim_in_subject_report": "sub3/sub4 heavy recompute submitted to cluster as cj1448", "measured": "cj1448 exists but terminal state=killed (submitted 11-13 01:55); no cluster artifact is cited in the report; sub3/sub4 numbers came from the local setsid route, which the report also states", "verdict": "claim is half-true and self-consistent (report says the local route produced the numbers first), but no cluster row backs the numbers; auditor reran sub3/sub4 locally AND resubmitted to the cluster (cj1466)"}, "F4_low_tracelevel_scope": {"consequence": "validates the exterior DtN/single-layer solution operator, not a general radiation solve -> level capped at L4, L5 not claimed", "meas